<title>UK: Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stock levels.</title>
<headline>Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stock levels.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil product inventories held in independent tankage in the Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp area were estimated to be at the following levels currently, a week ago and a year ago, industry sources said.</p>
<p>All figures in thousands of tonnes:</p>
<p>			20/2/97		  13/2/97	     23/2/96</p>
<p>    Gasoline	500-525			600	     550-575</p>
<p>    Naphtha		75		   75-100		    50</p>
<p>    Gas oil	   1,750		    1,750		 1,750</p>
<p>    Fuel oil	    400			350		   450</p>
<p>    Jet kero	     15			 15		    10</p>
<p>Naphtha stocks were broadly balanced with outgoing barges going into the German petrochemical industry. Gas oil was steady with incoming Russian cargoes offset by exports to Germany, Swizterland, Belgium and France.</p>
<p>Fuel oil stocks were higher with incoming straight run fuel oil partly balanced by outgoing barges moving similar product into Germany.</p>
<p>Jet kero stocks were steady with outgoing material moving to the aviation sector.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4984</p>
